EOF
sl --top 5; true
FINAL ANSWER:
Yes, two people appeared under more than one identity. I wrote the fixes to `.mailmap`, which git blame and the tool both read.

**Duplicates found**
- **Troy Goode** used two addresses: `<email redacted>` (93 commits) and `troy@laptop.example` (2 commits). The same name on two addresses is the only evidence.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades** used one address, `<email redacted>`, under two names: "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades" and "alex94puchades" (4 and 1 commits).

**Change made.** I added these lines to `.mailmap`, under the comment `# proposed by surviving-lines, confirm before relying on them`:
```
Troy Goode <<email redacted>> <troy@laptop.example>
Alejandro Caravaca Puchades <<email redacted>> alex94puchades <<email redacted>>
```
These merges are guesses from names and addresses. They stay guesses until you confirm each pair is one person.

**New top author, by surviving lines: Troy Goode, 810 lines (40.8%) and 95 commits (30.2%).** Before the merge, `<email redacted>` alone had 762 lines (38.4%) and 93 commits (29.5%). Troy Goode was already first before the merge, so the merge only widens the lead. Douglas Christopher Wilson is second with 629 lines (31.7%), but has the most commits at 143 (45.4%).

**Scope of these numbers**
- **Reformat commit:** the tool left out `62628c0`, "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes" by Fiona Formatter, dated 2026-04-12. It touched 291 lines. If you count it, Fiona Formatter would hold 291 lines (14.7%). Troy Goode would then have 715 lines (36.0%) and still be first.
- **Bots:** one bot identity was excluded (10 lines, 11 commits).
- **Bus factor:** 2 authors. Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson together hold 72.5% of the 1,985 surviving lines. It takes 4 authors to reach 80%. Both figures cover the whole repository, and bus factor here means the fewest authors whose lines add up to 50%.

The lines and commit counts cover all 18 files, with 1,985 of 1,995 lines attributed. They show whose code is still here, not code quality or review work.

